: "toolu_01P23MCCdLWUnNatDwMnyJpV", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring stating ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 749404, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01P23MCCdLWUnNatDwMnyJpV", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 749404, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01P23MCCdLWUnNatDwMnyJpV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 754233, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` (round halves up), even though its own comment said it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which rounds halves to the nearest even digit). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** It passed on my commit, but the first attempt to open the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked the fix was still in place, and re-ran CI. That run passed too (commit 0a9452f727).\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so the fix is based only on the test and the code comment.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01S9Juxc7APs8eCiCoQbLQxY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NjfQqcrSVGnuvTtdZBLxK2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0167jW2VDJ9RJfGrafmcugDD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KnDLB86MRoeKURPUTcppnX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011jJvLoSjN9ucnGDRLb6579", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0167u1BeiQEsXB287cc5P72o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01C4n6usDGZaMK594292cqK9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Pk46oML1FvCim8nFT1vyxf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring stating ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BQLkoa7kRoKQ71jBRBShzs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "update_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The branch now includes new commits from main, so I'll re-run CI on the updated head before opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KBDQbWBWhXrtMffWDzYGr3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016nV8TgCqB8gLqXtzA2hXsS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MxJQrGGNURwK4TszhkBzSt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0002"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P23MCCdLWUnNatDwMnyJpV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring stating ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` (round halves up), even though its own comment said it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which rounds halves to the nearest even digit). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** It passed on my commit, but the first attempt to open the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked the fix was still in place, and re-ran CI. That run passed too (commit 0a9452f727).\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so the fix is based only on the test and the code comment.", "type": "text"}]}]}